               <msContents>
                  <msItem n="1">
                     <title xml:lang="he-Latn-x-lc" key="work_289">Sefer ha-Mikhlol</title>
                     <title>ספר המכלול</title>
                     <author key="person_100213323">
                        <persName>Kimhi, David, approximately 1160-approximately 1235</persName>
                        <persName xml:lang="he">דוד בן יוסף קמחי</persName>
                     </author>
                     <note>Throughout the text, numerous superscript and marginal annotations and
                        corrections in tiny Sephardic cursive hands.</note>
                     <note>The ending is defective; the text terminates just before the end of the
                        section on numerals (the final words are <foreign xml:lang="he">יגמר המספר
                           בעצמו</foreign>).</note>
                     <textLang mainLang="he">Hebrew</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <physDesc>
                  <objectDesc form="codex">
                     <supportDesc material="chart">
                        <support>paper</support>
                        <extent n="199">ff. 199 <dimensions type="leaf" unit="mm">
                              <height>250</height>
                              <width>162</width>
                           </dimensions></extent>
                        <condition><p>Relatively extensive worm damage, especially on the outer
                              margins in the first half of the manuscript, some of which have been
                              repaired with small rectangular slips of paper. In some cases, this
                              affects the legibility of the text.</p></condition>
                     </supportDesc>
                  </objectDesc>
                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote>Oriental-Sephardic semi-cursive script, employing Sephardic cursive
                        forms</handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  <bindingDesc>
                     <p>Dark brown cloth over pasteboards, quarter-bound in dark brown fine-grained
                        leather. The author’s name (‘D. KIMCHI’) and the current shelfmark have been
                        gold-tooled on the spine.</p>
                  </bindingDesc>
